==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term/t|la|mediocritās}}, from {{term|mediocris}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/miːdɪˈɒkɹɪti/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|mediocrities}}

# {{context|now|_|rare|lang=en}} The quality of being [[intermediate]] between two extremes; a [[mean]].
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} A middle course of action; [[moderation]], [[balance]].
#* '''1621''', Robert Burton, ''The Anatomy of Melancholy'', New York Review Books 2001, p. 273:
#*: In adversity I wish for prosperity, and in prosperity I am afraid of adversity. What '''mediocrity''' may be found?
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The condition of being [[mediocre]]; having only an average degree of quality, skills etc.; no better than standard.
# An individual with mediocre abilities or achievements.

